| `no swallowed errors` | A bare `except:` or a broad handler that only drops the error fails `tests/integration/test_swallowed_error_gate.py` unless its `# noqa: BLE001` or `E722` gives a reason, and a suppression with a blank reason fails too; a narrow handler that only drops the error or puts a fixed value in its place, `contextlib.suppress(...)` and `ignore_errors=True` fail through `scripts/expiring_tier.py` unless a `# noqa: DROP001`, `DROP002` or `DROP003` gives a reason. | `make test` | — | It cannot see a handler that does work but never looks at the error. | [python-style.md](../guides/python-style.md) | always |
